Under [POL-AML-PRIV-2026-V4 / §203.1], Before taking adverse action based on a consumer report, the creditor must:
- Notify the consumer in writing of the adverse action and the right to a free credit report under [POL-FCRA-PRIV-2025-V7 / §607.11];
- Explain the specific reasons for the adverse action [POL-AML-PRIV-2026-V4 / §203.2];
- Provide the consumer with the name, address, and telephone number of the consumer reporting agency [POL-FCRA-PRIV-2025-V7 / §607.11];
- Offer the consumer an opportunity to resolve the dispute within 30 days of receiving the notice [POL-AML-PRIV-2026-V4 / §203.3].
